# trivy allowlist — CVEs accepted for the images CI scans.
#
# Consumed by ci.yml's `trivy` job, which fails on a CRITICAL twice over: with
# --ignore-unfixed (a fix in the image's own Debian release), and without it (a
# fix in ANY release, the bar adopters' mirror scanners hold us to), and by
# nightly.yml's `published-image-scan` of the images already published. It
# scans every image release.yml publishes — wardynd, wardyn-proxy, agent-base,
# agent-codex-cli, agent-aws-sso, agent-vscode and agent-novnc (#141), not just
# one of them. One CVE id per line; `#` starts a comment. Trivy applies this
# file verbatim — an id here is silenced everywhere, so keep the scope note in
# the comment.
#
# RULES for adding an entry (this file is a security exception log, not a mute
# button): every id needs a comment naming (1) the package, (2) WHY it does not
# reach us in this image, and (3) the date + who accepted it. An entry with no
# reason is a finding someone hid. Delete an entry the moment the base image
# ships a fix. The strict pass does not skip a no-fix-available CRITICAL, so an
# entry here is either one we could have patched and chose not to, or one no
# release of our base fixes yet — say which.

# openssh-client / openssh-sftp-server (every agent image). Use-after-free in
# ssh when a server changes its host key during a key re-exchange. No release
# of our base fixes it yet: Debian 13 carries 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u4, vulnerable,
# "minor issue, no DSA"; trixie-backports 10.3p1 is vulnerable too; the fix is
# 10.4p1+, in forky/sid only. Why it does not reach us: the bug is in the ssh
# client, and the only ssh client runs inside the sandbox as its unprivileged
# user (uid 1000), with egress only through the proxy; no control-plane code
# runs ssh (the SSH gateway uses sftp-server as a subsystem, not the client).
# At worst a malicious server crashes or subverts a client the run itself
# started. It was in every bookworm image too.
# Accepted 2026-09-30 by the owner for 0.8.3; delete when Debian 13 ships a fix.
CVE-2026-60002

# libxml2 (agent-novnc only). Use-after-free in xmlParseInternalSubset: a
# crafted XML document can crash the parsing process (denial of service). No
# release of our base fixes it yet: Debian 13 carries
# 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-2.1+deb13u3, vulnerable, "no DSA"; fixed in
# forky/sid only. Why it does not reach us: the worst case is the novnc
# sandbox's own process crashing on a document the run itself fed it; nothing
# outside the sandbox parses through it. Accepted 2026-09-30 by the owner for
# 0.8.3; delete when Debian 13 ships a fix.
CVE-2026-6653
